B9J08_000724	FUNCTION: Located at the top of the head of the 30S subunit, it contacts several helices of the 18S rRNA.
B9J08_000730	FUNCTION: Metallothionein involved in a wide variety of cellular processes, including protection of the proteome from stress, folding and transport of newly synthesized polypeptides, activation of proteolysis of misfolded proteins and the formation and dissociation of protein complexes.
B9J08_000783	FUNCTION: Required for efficient homologous chromosome segregation.
B9J08_000799	FUNCTION: Contains a zinc finger that can act as a transcriptional activator or repressor.
B9J08_000806	FUNCTION: Catalyzes the transfer of a phosphomonoester to a serine or threonine residue.
B9J08_000807	FUNCTION: Involved in the regulation of nitrogen metabolism. Up-regulates, in response to changes in intracellular N levels, the expression of a number of genes involved in nitrogen assimilation such as thioredoxin reductase, glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase and pyruvate dehydrogenase.
B9J08_000817	FUNCTION: Non-catalytic subunit of the obisolate reductase complex, a multiprotein complex that catalyzes the initial transfer of a defined glycan ManGlcNAc in eukaryotes) from the lipid carrier dolichol-pyrophosphate to an asparagine residue within an Asn-X-Ser/Thr consensus motif in ubiquitin chains, the first step in ubiquitin chain maturation. The complex also has a depalmitoyl transferase activity.
B9J08_000824	FUNCTION: Required for normal cell wall integrity and for the correct assembly of the mannoprotein outer layer of the cell wall. Important for apical-basal adhesion.
