B9J08_000891	FUNCTION: Plays a role in virion assembly and budding.
B9J08_000892	FUNCTION: Component of the outer cell wall layer. Required for stability of the cell wall and for optimal growth. Required during the transition from yeast to spore life span.
B9J08_000906	FUNCTION: Lysis-specific nuclease with a preference for pyrimidines, and acts on the 3' side of pyrimidine nucleotides. Possesses a phosphodiesterase activity.
B9J08_000911	FUNCTION: Inhibins and activins inhibit and activate, respectively, the secretion of follitropin by the pituitary gland. Inhibins/activins are involved in regulating a number of diverse functions such as hypothalamic and pituitary hormone secretion, gonadal hormone secretion, germ cell development and maturation, plant growth and development, or senescence.
