B9J08_001219	FUNCTION: Probably plays a role in symbiotic development.
B9J08_001223	FUNCTION: Converts protonucleotides and malonate semialdehydes to protonucleotides.
B9J08_001226	FUNCTION: This enzyme is involved in the biosynthesis of deoxyribonucleotides.
B9J08_001234	FUNCTION: Capsid protein p27: Self-associates to form the irregular polyhedron core composed of hexamers and pentamers, that encapsulates the genomic RNA-nucleocapsid complex. Aspartyl protease p27: self-associates to form the irregular polyhedron core composed of hexamers and pentamers, that encapsulates the genomic RNA-nucleocapsid complex. ; FUNCTION: : Mediates proteolytic cleavages of Gag and Gag-Pol polyproteins during or shortly after the release of the virion from the plasma membrane. Cleavages take place as an ordered, step-wise cascade to yield mature proteins. This process is called maturation. Displays maximal activity during the budding process just prior to particle release from the cell.
B9J08_001268	FUNCTION: This protein is an allosteric activator of the nitric oxide reductase.
B9J08_001287	FUNCTION: Catalyzes the hydrolysis of short-chain aliphatic nitriles to their corresponding organic acids with release of ammonia.
B9J08_001290	FUNCTION: This protein is an obisoluteute protein.
B9J08_001308	FUNCTION: Required for correct chromosome segregation.
B9J08_001313	FUNCTION: May only reduce GSH-thiol disulfides, but not protein disulfides.
