B9J08_001317	FUNCTION: This protein is an aliphatic nitrogenase.
B9J08_001321	FUNCTION: Probably serves as a microtubule-dependent and Rho-type motility sensor.
B9J08_001339	FUNCTION: Forms a fibrillar layer on the bacterial surface that provides a framework for the olfactory epithelial to meso-diaminopimelic acid layer.
B9J08_001341	FUNCTION: Heavy-metal-binding protein. Binds one copper per subunit.
B9J08_001342	FUNCTION: Positive-regulator of glutamine synthetase.
B9J08_001361	FUNCTION: Acts as a transcriptional regulator. Binds to and activates the promoter of the hairy genes YCRF1, YCRF2 and YCRF3.
B9J08_001370	FUNCTION: Probable serine/threonine-protein phosphatase which may play a role in cell cycle regulation.
B9J08_001426	FUNCTION: Cell surface adhesion protein that mediates both yeast-to-host tissue adherence and yeast aggregation. Plays an important role in the pathogenesis of C.albicans infections.
B9J08_001437	FUNCTION: The cytochrome b5/NADH cytochrome b5 reductases are involved in desaturation and elongation of fatty acids, cholesterol biosynthesis, drug metabolism, and, in erythrocyte, methemoglobin reduction. They oxidize a variety of structurally unrelated compounds, including steroids, fatty acids, and xenobiotics.
B9J08_001440	FUNCTION: Recruits the G-protein coupled glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenases glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase and glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase to the glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase promoter. Promotes the activation of the glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydratases gprA and gprB, as well as the glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase gprD and the glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase gprC. Positively regulates the activity of the glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydratase gprE.
B9J08_001441	FUNCTION: Acts as a guanine nucleotide exchange factor for RDH1, RHO2 and RHO3. Promotes the exchange of GDP to GTP, converting inactive GDP-bound RHO1 into its active GTP-bound form.
