B9J08_001459	FUNCTION: This protein is an aliphatic monooxygenase.
B9J08_001466	FUNCTION: Involved in spore wall assembly, sex determination and cell division. May be involved in a reorganization of the cytoskeleton during sporulation.
B9J08_001468	FUNCTION: The octamer is a protein that binds to and probably organizes the N-terminal part of nascent peptide chains.
B9J08_001470	FUNCTION: Probably involved in the organization of the cytoskeleton. May link microtubules to the actin cytoskeleton.
B9J08_001472	FUNCTION: This protein is an obissile protein that can act as a molecular chaperone to guide and/or transport proteins in the secretory pathway.
B9J08_001479	FUNCTION: May play a role as a scaffolding protein in plastids.
